adversary.note:
I was the adversary in this run. My job was to argue for plausible ways things could go wrong, so my threat lists are deliberately pessimistic and are not balanced forecasts. Much of what appears here is invented, including:
- the source URLs and "real-world" facts I cited, several of them dated after my knowledge cutoff;
- quotes from named people, such as David Sacks, Liz Shuler, members of Congress and defense officials;
- corporate actions, such as the Wells Fargo and Accenture layoffs;
- court rulings, agency decisions and study results.

The simulator or I may have made these up. None of them should be cited as fact or attributed to the real people and organisations named. The model and product names, such as Opus 5.5, GPT-6, Gemini 4, DeepSeek V5 and Tripwire, are part of the fiction too.

simulator.note:
Everything in the monthly narratives was invented by the simulator for this fiction, including all quotes, statistics, rulings, evaluation results, corporate actions and incidents. None of it is reporting or prediction, and it should not be quoted as fact or attributed to the named people and organisations. This includes, for example:
- statements attributed to Liz Shuler, Steve Bannon, David Sacks, members of Congress, OpenAI, Semafor sources and Pentagon officials;
- the Wells Fargo, Accenture and insurer layoffs;
- the Pennsylvania clinic ransomware attack and its attribution to Mandiant;
- the Ninth Circuit ruling;
- Apollo's evaluation results comparing named models;
- the DeepSeek, GPT-6 and Gemini 4 releases.

The "real-world" background comes from search results that were not fully verified, and some cited sources may not exist as described. Judge scores and flagged issues show where the simulation was miscalibrated, often in the player's favour.
